| clean constant pixel | mean corrupted pixel, sigma 0.35 |
|---:|---:|
| 0.0 | 0.139994 |
| 0.5 | 0.500481 |
| 1.0 | 0.860566 |
\image(figures/denoising_conditional_risk.svg)
// result_end

\caption(When both clean possibilities have the same observed value, their squared-error optimum is the conditional average. The red point is the result of six visible SGD updates.)
\alttext(A quadratic risk curve has its minimum at prediction one half and risk one quarter, with the fitted point close to that minimum.)

The positive mean at clean zero and negative mean shift at clean one follow from clipping, not
from a nonzero Gaussian mean. A clipped observation's error distribution depends on its clean
value. A formula for unbounded additive Gaussian observations cannot simply be substituted for
this clipped corruption process.

> The original network, executed

The model is the same strict undercomplete network as the
[undercomplete example](undercomplete_autoencoder.mepml): 784 inputs, 32 ReLU code values and
784 sigmoid outputs. Its independent encoder and decoder contain 50,992 scalars in four tensors.
It uses Glorot-uniform weights and zero biases. Denoising changes the training pairs and loss
target, not this architecture. The single-image trace uses Flow style and layer detail, shared
linear shape scales, a two-pixel visibility floor and at most six sampled planes. The symbols
represent tensors rather than individually drawn neurons. This probe is not another fit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/denoising_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1657);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& input) {
        return n::models::UndercompleteAutoencoder(p, input).reconstruction;
      },
      "Denoising forward path: 784 to 32 ReLU to 784 sigmoid");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Layers;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 50992 || p.size() != 4 || figure.parameter_count() != 50992)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  figure.save_svg("build/denoising_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} learned tensors; {} learned scalars. Inference takes the observed image only.\n",
      p.size(),
      p.count());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
4 learned tensors; 50992 learned scalars. Inference takes the observed image only.
\image(figures/denoising_architecture.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The target branch belongs to the training objective, not the inference graph. The ordinary control uses exactly the same forward architecture.)
\alttext(An executed dense architecture maps 784 observed pixels through 32 ReLU coordinates to 784 sigmoid outputs.)

> Genuine MNIST and explicit noise banks

The native dataset API prepares 1,000 fitting, 200 validation and 200 held-out MNIST images,
with equal class counts in each pool. It retains the official original IDs, disjoint fitting and
validation rows from the original training split and held-out rows from the original test split.
Labels only order the gallery. Images are Float32 NHWC [N,28,28,1] in [0,1]. The code saves the
manifest, clean pools, source IDs and all fixed evaluation banks.

Validation uses seed 1709, the main test seed 1711 and the second test seed 1717. The main noise
level is Float32 0.35. Low (0.15) and strong (0.6) cases reuse the main test's standard draws,
so only amplitude changes. Clean inputs have sigma zero. Independent local MT19937 engines
and explicit cosine/sine Box-Muller pairs preserve the source stream; these differ from the
library's ordinary `normal` sampler. No Python preparation or framework training is involved.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto pools           = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  const auto validation_bank = n::models::GaussianNoise(pools[1].images.shape(), 1, 1709);
  const auto test_bank       = n::models::GaussianNoise(pools[2].images.shape(), 1, 1711);
  const auto second_bank     = n::models::GaussianNoise(pools[2].images.shape(), 1, 1717);
  const auto validation = n::models::CorruptForDenoising(pools[1].images, validation_bank, .35f);
  const auto test       = n::models::CorruptForDenoising(pools[2].images, test_bank, .35f);
  n::save_npz(
      "build/denoising_data.npz",
      {{"fit_images", pools[0].images},
       {"validation_images", pools[1].images},
       {"test_images", pools[2].images},
       {"fit_source_ids", pools[0].source},
       {"validation_source_ids", pools[1].source},
       {"test_source_ids", pools[2].source},
       {"test_labels", pools[2].labels},
       {"validation_standard_noise", validation_bank},
       {"test_standard_noise", test_bank},
       {"second_standard_noise", second_bank},
       {"validation_corrupted", validation},
       {"test_corrupted", test},
       {"test_low", n::models::CorruptForDenoising(pools[2].images, test_bank, .15f)},
       {"test_strong", n::models::CorruptForDenoising(pools[2].images, test_bank, .6f)},
       {"test_second", n::models::CorruptForDenoising(pools[2].images, second_bank, .35f)}});
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/denoising_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("| pool | images | pixels per image | examples per digit |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | 784 | {} |\n",
        i == 0   ? "fit"
        : i == 1 ? "validation"
                 : "test",
        pools[i].images.size(0),
        pools[i].images.size(0) / 10);
}
```
